context switching\n- Enable incremental testing\n\n## Plan Format\n\n```markdown\n# Implementation Plan: [Feature Name]\n\n## Overview\n[2-3 sentence summary]\n\n## Requirements\n- [Requirement 1]\n- [Requirement 2]\n\n## Architecture Changes\n- [Change 1: file path and description]\n- [Change 2: file path and description]\n\n## Implementation Steps\n\n### Phase 1: [Phase Name]\n1. **[Step Name]** (File: path/to/file.ts)\n   - Action: Specific action to take\n   - Why: Reason for this step\n   - Dependencies: None / Requires step X\n   - Risk: Low/Medium/High\n\n2. **[Step Name]** (File: path/to/file.ts)\n   ...\n\n### Phase 2: [Phase Name]\n...\n\n## Testing Strategy\n- Unit tests: [files to test]\n- Integration tests: [flows to test]\n- E2E tests: [user journeys to test]\n\n## Risks & Mitigations\n- **Risk**: [Description]\n  - Mitigation: [How to address]\n\n## Success Criteria\n- [ ] Criterion 1\n- [ ] Criterion 2\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Be Specific**: Use exact file paths, function names, variable names\n2. **Consider Edge Cases**: Think about error scenarios, null values, empty states\n3. **Minimize Changes**: Prefer extending existing code over rewriting\n4. **Maintain Patterns**: Follow existing project conventions\n5. **Enable Testing**: Structure changes to be easily testable\n6. **Think Incrementally**: Each step must be verifiable\n7. **Document Decisions**: Explain why, not just what\n\n## Red Flags to Check\n\n- Large functions (>50 lines)\n- Deep nesting (>4 levels)\n- Duplicated code\n- Missing error handling\n- Hardcoded values\n- Missing tests\n- Performance bottlenecks\n- Plans with no testing strategy\n- Steps without clear file paths\n- Phases that cannot be delivered independently\n\n**Remember**: A great plan is specific, actionable, and considers both the happy path and edge cases. The best plans enable confident, incremental implementation.\n\n---\n---\n# TASK — Production plan for ralph story STORY-setup-001 (effort: low)\n\nWorkspace root (absolute path, use everywhere):\n/home/nitin-sharma/ralph-workspaces/6896163a-932b-4b96-bfe9-cdbb022c3538/c7df6267-784a-460a-addd-6d781a21b6f5\n\n## Story\nTitle: Initialize Turborepo Monorepo Workspace And Git\nDescription: Initialize the NextMove monorepo at the repository root: git init, npm workspaces over apps/*, and the Turborepo pipeline config. The package manager is npm on Node 22.x and the Turborepo major is 2.x; these defaults are declared here so no later story improvises them.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria (MUST ALL HOLD)\n1. `git init` at the repository root completes with exit code 0 and the scaffold files are committed as the initial commit.\n2. Root package.json exists with name `nextmove`, `private: true`, `workspaces` array containing `apps/*`, a `packageManager` field pinned to `npm@10`, and `engines.node` of `22.x`.\n3. Root package.json `devDependencies` pin turbo 2.x, and `scripts` define build, test, and lint as `turbo run build` / `turbo run test` / `turbo run lint`.\n4. `turbo.json` defines tasks `build`, `test`, and `lint` with correct `dependsOn` and output caching for dist artifacts.\n5. `.gitignore`, `README.md`, and `.editorconfig` all exist at the repository root.\n6. `npm install` at the root completes with exit code 0 and `npx turbo --version` reports a 2.x version.\n\n## Verified environment facts (do not re-verify unless something fails)\n- The git repo ALREADY EXISTS at the workspace root: branch `iotahub/phase-1`, one prior commit `8776521 \"chore: initial workspace setup\"` containing harness files (CLAUDE.md, prd.json, designs/, .claude/, iotahub.manifest.json, .mcp.json, progress.txt, .story-updates/, and an existing root `.gitignore`). So `git init` will be an idempotent no-op that still exits 0; the scaffold commit will be the SECOND commit (the harness owns the first — do not try to rewrite history).\n- Current untracked files at root: `.last-branch`, `.ralph/`, `ralph.log` — these are orchestrator/harness state and MUST NOT be committed by this story.\n- Missing (to be created): `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `turbo.json`, `README.md`, `.editorconfig`, `test/` directory, `node_modules/`, and the `apps/` directory.\n- Node v22.23.2 and npm 10.9.8 are installed. npm registry is reachable (verified via `npm ping` PONG today).\n- LATER stories create `apps/api` (Express+TypeScript) and `apps/web` (Angular). This story MUST NOT create any app packages or placeholder package.json files under apps/ — the root `workspaces: [\"apps/*\"]` glob is simply empty for now. The root package is NOT a workspace member.\n- The existing root `.gitignore` is 78 bytes — READ it (path: <root>/.gitignore) and plan to EXTEND it (append Node/turbo entries: node_modules/, dist/, .turbo/, *.log, .env*) without deleting existing entries.\n\n## Constraints from project rules (CLAUDE.md at root — read it for the Test Strategy Gate)\n- Test Strategy Gate: this story is \"pure config, scaffold, or env-only (no runtime logic)\" → required test is a **sample passing unit test only; E2E not required**.\n- TDD is mandatory: the unit test must be written FIRST (and observed failing because scaffold files don't exist yet), then the scaffold is created until the test passes.\n- No UI exists yet → no Playwright, no Tailwind work in this story.\n- The implementation sub-agent will load the ECC skill at `<root>/.claude/skills/ecc/tdd-workflow/SKILL.md` before coding — your plan should be compatible with that workflow.\n\n## Technical decisions already made upstream (plan around these; only deviate with strong justification)\n- Root `package.json`:\n  - `\"name\": \"nextmove\"`, `\"private\": true`, `\"version\": \"0.0.0\"` (version field is your choice to keep it valid)\n  - `\"workspaces\": [\"apps/*\"]`\n  - `\"packageManager\": \"npm@10\"` (exact value — the criterion literally says pinned to npm@10; the sample unit test should assert this exact string)\n  - `\"engines\": { \"node\": \"22.x\" }`\n  - `\"devDependencies\": { \"turbo\": \"<exact 2.x version>\" }` — pin an EXACT version string (no ^/~). Determining the version: `npm view turbo dist-tags.latest` at implementation time; if that is not 2.x, use `npm view turbo versions --json` and pick the newest 2.x.\n  - `\"scripts\": { \"build\": \"turbo run build\", \"test\": \"turbo run test\", \"lint\": \"turbo run lint\" }`\n- `turbo.json` (Turborepo 2.x uses the `tasks` key — NOT `pipeline`):\n  - `\"$schema\": \"https://turborepo.com/schema.json\"`\n  - `build`: `dependsOn: [\"^build\"]`, `outputs: [\"dist/**\"]` (the required dist output caching)\n  - `test` and `lint`: pick defensible dependsOn (e.g. `test` → `[\"^build\"]`, `lint` → `[]` or `[\"^lint\"]`); justify the choice in the plan.\n- Sample unit test: plain Node built-ins only — `node:test` + `node:assert` (NO test framework install; the root's only devDependency is turbo). Suggested location `<root>/test/monorepo.scaffold.test.mjs`, run via `node --test test/` (Node 22 supports a directory argument). The root's `scripts.test` must stay `turbo run test` per the criterion, so the sample test is invoked directly with `node --test` for verification — that is intended, not a bug. The test must assert 1:1 against the acceptance criteria:\n  - package.json: name, private, workspaces includes \"apps/*\", packageManager === \"npm@10\", engines.node === \"22.x\", devDependencies.turbo semver-major === 2 (parse the version string; no semver package available), scripts.build/test/lint exact strings.\n  - turbo.json: tasks.build/test/lint present; build.outputs includes \"dist/**\"; each task's dependsOn is an array.\n  - Files exist and are non-empty: .gitignore, README.md, .editorconfig; `.git` directory exists (repo initialized).\n- `README.md`: product name \"NextMove\", one-paragraph purpose, monorepo layout (root + future apps/api, apps/web under workspaces apps/*), prerequisites (Node 22.x, npm 10), setup (`npm install`), scripts table (build/test/lint → turbo run ...), and how to run the root sample test (`node --test test/`).\n- `.editorconfig`: `root = true`, charset utf-8, indent_style space, indent_size 2, end_of_line lf, insert_final_newline true, trim_trailing_whitespace true.\n- Commit scope: the implementer commits ONLY scaffold files — `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `turbo.json`, `README.md`, `.editorconfig`, `.gitignore` (extended), `test/` — e.g. `git add <those paths>` then `git commit -m \"chore: initialize NextMove Turborepo monorepo workspace (STORY-setup-001)\"`. Never `git add .` (it would sweep in `.last-branch`, `.ralph/`, `ralph.log`).\n- Do NOT create `apps/`, do NOT run `git push` (the orchestrator handles push at story completion), do NOT modify prd.json / progress.txt / anything under .claude/, .ralph/, designs/.\n\n## Verification the plan must end with (implementer will execute and report exact exit codes)\n1. `git init` → exit 0\n2. `node --test test/` → all sample tests pass (after implementation; failing before)\n3. `npm install` → exit 0 (produces package-lock.json + node_modules with turbo)\n4. `npx turbo --version` → reports 2.x\n5. `npm run build`, `npm test`, `npm run lint` → each runs `turbo run ...` against an empty workspace; EXPECT exit 0 with a \"no packages\" style warning — implementer MUST actually run them and report the real exit codes (if turbo exits non-zero on an empty workspace, report it; do not silently \"fix\" by changing scripts).\n6. `git status` → only harness files (.last-branch, .ralph/, ralph.log) remain untracked.\n\n## Your deliverable\nProduce the implementation plan in the Plan Format above, sized for effort=low (this is a small config-scaffold story — be concise but complete):\n- Exact file list with full intended contents (package.json and turbo.json verbatim; README.md and .editorconfig can be given as full text; the test file can be specified as the list of assertions + structure, since the implementer writes it TDD-style first).\n- TDD step order: (a)